  "version": 1,
  "title": "Cardinalities of three-point ordered convolution-square fibres",
  "abstract": "In any finite abelian group G, fix a three-element support S and retain the entire labelled ordered additive convolution square, including diagonal pairs. The number of three-element supports with the same square is h or 2h, where h is the number of elements u satisfying u+u=0; in particular it is at most 2h. The full proof is included. This adapts a prior public Couret formalization; novelty and independent human review are not established.",
